f an element.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"color"},{"name":"halign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different. The most typical case is for credits, such as:"}]}]},{"name":"valign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"placement","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation."}]}]},{"name":"underline","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The number of lines used to underline the text: ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (none), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"overline","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The number of lines used to overline the text: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":" (none), ","type":"text"},{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"lineThrough","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of lines used to strike through the text: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":" (none), ","type":"text"},{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"2","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":"3","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"name":"enclosure","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The enclosure attribute group is used to specify the formatting of an enclosure around text or symbols."}]}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/init(id:items:position:font:color:halign:valign:placement:underline:overline:lineThrough:enclosure:)"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"title":"MXLFont","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics/Item":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics\/item","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/Item","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"One of the alternatives for Dynamics.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLDynamics.Item"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Dynamics can be associated either with a note or a general musical direction. To avoid inconsistencies between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and among the letter abbreviations for dynamics (what is sf vs. sfz, standing alone or with a trailing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic that is not always piano), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to create marks not covered by a single element, such as sfmp.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLDynamics"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlabovebelow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The above-below type is used to indicate whether one element appears above or below another element.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"title":"MXLAboveBelow"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","i